# Unit-test time limits per module, in ms (the test runner in
# source/nano/testenv_test.d fails a module that takes longer; the default
# limit is 1000 ms). A module is listed only when its tests must wait on real
# processes, sockets or timeouts; say why. Shorten the waits before raising a
# limit: make the timeout or grace period a parameter, or use nano.clock's
# FakeClock. NANO_TEST_BUDGET_SCALE multiplies every limit (slow machines).
nano.claude_hooks 4000 real hook processes run into their timeouts
nano.providers.openai_test 3000 a stream must outlast the 1 s idle timeout
nano.http 3000 real sockets: refused, stalled and redirected connections
nano.providers.anthropic_test 2500 scripted streaming server with drip delays
nano.keycmd 2500 key commands run into their timeouts and drain grace
nano.context 6000 the bounded-pin-stash test renders thousands of requests at several windows
nano.session 5000 the bounded-pin-stash restore tests build and parse ~3,000-request JSON logs
nano.agent_resume_test 3000 the bounded-pin-stash round-trip compacts and resumes a ~3,000-request session
